 1 . Amstrong Number :

import java.util.Scanner;

public class ArmstrongNumber {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input number
        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        int num = sc.nextInt();

        // Copy for checking later
        int original = num;
        int result = 0;

        // Count digits
        int n = String.valueOf(num).length();

        // Calculate sum of powers of digits
        while (num > 0) {
            int digit = num % 10;         // get last digit
            result += Math.pow(digit, n); // add digit^n
            num /= 10;                    // remove last digit
        }

        // Check Armstrong condition
        if (result == original) {
            System.out.println(original + " is an Armstrong number.");
        } else {
            System.out.println(original + " is NOT an Armstrong number.");
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}
Enter a number: 153
153 is an Armstrong number.


2.Palindrome :
import java.util.Scanner;

public class PalindromeNumber {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input number
        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        int num = sc.nextInt();

        int original = num;
        int reversed = 0;

        // Reverse the number
        while (num > 0) {
            int digit = num % 10;          // extract last digit
            reversed = reversed * 10 + digit; // build reversed number
            num /= 10;                     // remove last digit
        }

        // Check palindrome condition
        if (original == reversed) {
            System.out.println(original + " is a Palindrome number.");
        } else {
            System.out.println(original + " is NOT a Palindrome number.");
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}

Enter a number: 121
121 is a Palindrome number.


3. Print all the divisors of number 
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Divisors {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input number
        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.println("Divisors of " + n + " are:");

        // Loop through and check divisors
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            if (n % i == 0) {
                System.out.print(i + " ");
            }
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}

Enter a number: 28
Divisors of 28 are:
1 2 4 7 14 28

import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.TreeSet;

public class OptimizedDivisors {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input number
        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        // Using TreeSet to keep divisors sorted automatically
        TreeSet<Integer> divisors = new TreeSet<>();

        // Loop only till sqrt(n)
        for (int i = 1; i * i <= n; i++) {
            if (n % i == 0) {
                divisors.add(i);        // add divisor
                divisors.add(n / i);    // add pair divisor
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Divisors of " + n + " are: " + divisors);

        sc.close();
    }
}
Enter a number: 28
Divisors of 28 are: [1, 2, 4, 7, 14, 28]



